From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Copilot <copilot@github.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi: a80: Fix MMC reset entries to use RESET() not GATE()

The a80_mmc_resets[] array incorrectly used the GATE() macro instead of
RESET(). The GATE() macro does not set the CCU_RST_F_IS_VALID flag, so
reset_deassert() silently does nothing ("unhandled") for all four MMC
controller resets.

This means the mmc_config_clk (mmc-common) reset signal for each MMC
controller is never deasserted by the DM driver, causing U-Boot proper
to print:
  sunxi_set_reset: (RST#N) unhandled

Fix all four entries to use RESET() so the hardware reset registers are
correctly written during probe.

Signed-off-by: Copilot <copilot@github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi/clk_a80.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi/clk_a80.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi/clk_a80.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi/clk_a80.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi/clk_a80.c
@@ -77,10 +77,10 @@ static const struct ccu_clk_gate a80_mmc_gates[] = {
 };
 
 static const struct ccu_reset a80_mmc_resets[] = {
-	[0]			= GATE(0x0, BIT(18)),
-	[1]			= GATE(0x4, BIT(18)),
-	[2]			= GATE(0x8, BIT(18)),
-	[3]			= GATE(0xc, BIT(18)),
+	[0]			= RESET(0x0, BIT(18)),
+	[1]			= RESET(0x4, BIT(18)),
+	[2]			= RESET(0x8, BIT(18)),
+	[3]			= RESET(0xc, BIT(18)),
 };
 
 const struct ccu_desc a80_ccu_desc = {
